course: dictionary
lesson: 12246
title: A formal word for the police
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal: they sound grown-up, and you hear them in official places, like on signs and in news reports. Constabulary is one of them. Look at the words around it. «The county constabulary caught the thief after a long chase.» A thief is caught by people whose job is to enforce the law, so constabulary must mean the police.
explain: Look at the word's parts. Constable is an old word for a police officer, and the ending -ary often means a group of people linked to something. So a constabulary is the group of police officers for an area. Test your meaning in the sentence: «The local constabulary put up a notice asking for witnesses.» Police fits perfectly.
explain: The word is used most in Britain and Ireland. You might see «Lancashire Constabulary» on a police car. The important part is the area: each constabulary looks after one place, such as a county.
fact: Constabulary means the police force of an area.
fact: «Constabulary» is a formal word, used most in the UK and Ireland.
fact: «Lancashire Constabulary» is the police force for Lancashire, a county in England.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is taken before the court by the police, and stories call the local police the constabulary.
fact: The Royal Irish Constabulary was a police force in Ireland before 1922.
exercise: «The county constabulary caught the thief after a long chase.» What does constabulary mean here? | *The police force of the county | A long walk in the country | A group of cows in a field | A kind of court with a judge
exercise: On police cars you may read «Lancashire Constabulary». What does the name tell you? | A shop that sells cars | *It is the police force for Lancashire | A school for young artists | A famous castle in Lancashire
exercise: Which word means the police force of an area? | Carnival | Cathedral | *Constabulary | Cabinet
test: «The constabulary asked the crowd to stand back.» Who is the constabulary in this sentence? | The town mayor's family | A group of singers | *The police | The school's head teacher
test: Which sentence uses constabulary correctly? | The constabulary ate a big sandwich at lunch. | The constabulary played in the football match. | The constabulary is a type of cloud. | *The constabulary searched the woods for the missing dog.
exam: Liam says constabulary is a word for a shop. Why is he wrong? | Constabulary is a kind of food | Shops do not have names in Britain | The sentence is about a shop selling bread | *The context shows people who catch thieves, so it means police
